<!--
    Meizu MX6 (m95) - carrier config overrides, read by CarrierConfig after the
    per-carrier asset (DefaultCarrierConfigService.java:180-183: "Treat vendor.xml
    as if it were appended to the carrier config file we read"), filtered on the
    SIM's MCC/MNC.  There is no MegaFon asset in packages/apps/CarrierConfig, so
    for 250/02 this block is applied on top of the platform defaults.

    carrier_volte_available_bool: the platform default is false, and on 18.1 it
    was measured false for 25002 (`dumpsys carrier_config`, A11_BRINGUP_STATE.md
    section 2r) and then overridden by hand with `cmd phone cc set-value -p`,
    which lives in /data and is gone after a data wipe.  In the telephony stack
    its one consumer is ImsManager.isVolteEnabledByPlatform()
    (frameworks/opt/net/ims ImsManager.java:813-816), which
    persist.dbg.volte_avail_ovr=1 (system.prop) already short-circuits; stating
    it here makes the image stop depending on that debug property and makes
    Settings show the VoLTE switch for the right reason.

    Deliberately NOT set (defaults kept): carrier_vt_available_bool (ViLTE is not
    ported), carrier_wfc_ims_available_bool (ePDG is off,
    persist.mtk_epdg_support=0), carrier_supports_ss_over_ut_bool (the port does
    not carry UT/XCAP), carrier_volte_provisioned_bool (deprecated on Android 13,
    CarrierConfigManager.java:175-183, UCE only).
-->
<carrier_config_list>
    <carrier_config mcc="250" mnc="02">
        <boolean name="carrier_volte_available_bool" value="true" />
    </carrier_config>
</carrier_config_list>
